# The privacy tier. Never committed: the source's identity is a SHA-256 in
# params.yaml, and the PII placeholder map lives here (I13).
data/raw/

# Artifacts. Git tracks none of them; the run manifest records their digests, which
# is what makes a release identifiable without committing what it wrote. Listed per
# tier rather than as `data/`, so a tier can be un-ignored on its own. `run.json` is
# a file rather than a tier -- one run, one manifest, at the root of what it wrote.
data/interim/
data/processed/
data/release/
data/quarantine/
data/run.json
*.jsonl
!tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl

# Per-model LLM settings, read at the edge through `agent-toolkit`'s
# `JsonDirConfigResolver` (`<model>.json`, the convention it preserves). Never committed:
# a file naming an endpoint and holding a key is what AGENTS.md section 9 forbids, and the
# library's own YAML resolver refuses both keys for the same reason. `LLM_API_KEY` and
# `LLM_BASE_URL` are the environment's; what a model *does* -- temperature, ceilings --
# belongs in a committed policy file whose digest reaches the run manifest.
config/model/

# The default question store, for a developer who attached no database (Decision 7). It holds
# questions about real records, which makes a committed one a corpus in the repository. A
# deployment names its own through `DATAFORCE_DATABASE_URL` and never lands here.
dataforce.sqlite3

.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
